{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"thm-1-2","type":"text","text":"**Thm 1.12** \n==$A : n \\times n$==, the following conditions are equivalent.","x":-720,"y":-360,"width":480,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"**How to read the arrows**\n- Red →: the board proves this direction; the other direction follows by going around the arrows.\n- Green ⟷: the board proves both directions.\n- $H$: the reduced row-echelon form of $A$.","x":520,"y":-400,"width":480,"height":200},
		{"id":"c8","type":"text","text":"**(8)** $\\operatorname{rank}(A) = n$","x":-120,"y":-330,"width":240,"height":60},
		{"id":"c1","type":"text","text":"**(1)** $A$ is invertible","x":-600,"y":-30,"width":240,"height":60},
		{"id":"c2","type":"text","text":"**(2)** $\\forall\\, b \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times 1}$, $Ax = b$ has a unique solution","x":-170,"y":-50,"width":340,"height":100},
		{"id":"c7","type":"text","text":"**(7)** $\\forall\\, b \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times 1}$, $Ax = b$ has a solution","x":360,"y":-50,"width":320,"height":100},
		{"id":"c3","type":"text","text":"**(3)** $Ax = 0$ has only the trivial solution $x = 0$","x":-160,"y":240,"width":320,"height":100},
		{"id":"c4","type":"text","text":"**(4)** $A \\overset{r}{\\sim} I$","x":-100,"y":550,"width":200,"height":60},
		{"id":"c5","type":"text","text":"**(5)** $A$ can be expressed as a product of row-elementary matrices","x":-650,"y":530,"width":340,"height":100},
		{"id":"gaps","type":"text","text":"**Steps the board skips**\n- (1)⇒(2): also $A(A^{-1}b) = (AA^{-1})b = b$, so a solution exists.\n- (2)⇒(3): $0$ is a solution and the solution is unique, so $x = 0$ is the only one.\n- (3)⇒(4), (7)⇒(4): $H$ is $n \\times n$ and $H \\ne I$ ⇒ the last row of $H$ is $0$.\n- (7)⇒(4): $PA = H$ with $P$ invertible; choose $b = P^{-1}e_n$, then $c = e_n$.\n- (8)⇒(2): $\\operatorname{rank}(A) = n$ ⇒ $\\operatorname{rank}([A \\mid b]) = n$ for every $b$.","x":520,"y":490,"width":600,"height":300},
		{"id":"c6","type":"text","text":"**(6)** The span of the column vectors of $A$ is $\\mathbb{R}^{n \\times 1}$","x":760,"y":120,"width":320,"height":100}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"e-1-2","fromNode":"c1","fromSide":"right","toNode":"c2","toSide":"left","color":"1","label":"x = A⁻¹b"},
		{"id":"e-2-3","fromNode":"c2","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"c3","toSide":"top","color":"1","label":"let b = 0"},
		{"id":"e-3-4","fromNode":"c3","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"c4","toSide":"top","color":"1","label":"H ≠ I ⇒ infinitely many (→←)"},
		{"id":"e-4-5","fromNode":"c4","fromSide":"left","toNode":"c5","toSide":"right","color":"1","label":"E_k⋯E_1 A = I"},
		{"id":"e-5-1","fromNode":"c5","fromSide":"top","toNode":"c1","toSide":"bottom","color":"1","label":"product of invertible matrices"},
		{"id":"e-2-7","fromNode":"c2","fromSide":"right","toNode":"c7","toSide":"left","color":"1","label":"unique ⇒ exists"},
		{"id":"e-7-4","fromNode":"c7","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"c4","toSide":"right","color":"1","label":"H ≠ I ⇒ choose b (→←)"},
		{"id":"e-2-8","fromNode":"c2","fromSide":"top","toNode":"c8","toSide":"bottom","fromEnd":"arrow","color":"4","label":"rank(A) = rank([A|b]) = n"},
		{"id":"cf3c20191aa9cf8a","fromNode":"c6","fromSide":"top","toNode":"c7","toSide":"right","fromEnd":"arrow","color":"4","label":"Ax = combination of columns"}
	]
}